From 20d4aea5e8c4a8a7c6ef2293c16269b6bc5cdda1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabe Ochoa <urgentcactus@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:38:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Font fallback chains, visible replacements, and one
 styled-text layout

A glyph the primary face lacks is measured and drawn from the first face in
its fallback chain, inside measure_text and draw_text_ex, so every path that
measures or draws agrees. sokol uses fontstash's per-glyph fallback (plus
fonsResetFallbackFont from upstream so a chain can be replaced); raylib has
none, so place_glyphs lays out such strings for both measure and draw.
load_font_face loads one face of a .ttc on both backends, and system_fonts
lists the OS faces worth chaining (macOS verified, Linux/Windows paths only).

Codepoints no chained face covers draw as one visible replacement each
(U+FFFD if a face has it, else '?'), measured as drawn; ZWJ sequences and
flags collapse to one, uncovered modifiers vanish. Colour emoji are not
drawn: stb_truetype has no sbix/CBDT support.

TextSpan gains font and size_scale. layout_styled_text is the layout both
label renderers draw and Dim::Text measures, built on detail::line_x_at, the
pen a single draw call uses for each glyph. Wrap, ellipsis (styled labels now
truncate), run offsets and selection all come from it. Wrapping breaks
between ideographs.

Tests: text_fallback_test (sokol, captured glyph quads, 91 checks),
styled_text_test (both renderers, 28), text_fallback_raylib_test (headless
pixels, 26). text_memo_test's run offsets move to the pen positions.
